@ 6.2.2.1.10 - Classical Arabic to Hassāniyya Arabic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hass%C4%81n%C4%ABya
	# NB: Words borrowed directly from CA/MSA seem to be immune to these changes. Also, unless otherwise noted, changes also apply to geminate consonants.
	dˤ q > ðˤ ɡ
	f θ > v z̪
	ʔ > {∅,j,w}
	x > χ
	ɣ:[+ long] > ʁ:[+ long]
	ʁ:[+ long] > q:[+ long]
	ɣ > {ʁ,q}
	V:[- long] > ∅ / C_{C,#}
	aj aw > e:[+ long](ʲ) o:[+ long](ʷ)
	j w > i u / #_CV
	j w > i:[+ long] u:[+ long] / #_CC